t that=E2=80=99s small consolation =0Afor Republicans, because they have ma=
ny more of them to defend. Once again, the =0Amoney tells a clear story: Th=
e 22 most expensive House races are all districts =0ATrump won two years ag=
o. In six of those, combined spending has already =0Aeclipsed $10 million.=
=0A=0AAt the top of the list is Colorado=E2=80=99s 8th District race betwee=
n freshman =0ARepublican incumbent Gabe Evans and former state Representati=
ve Manny Rutinel. =0AIt=E2=80=99s a template of what=E2=80=99s happening in=
 many districts across the country. In =0A2024, Evans rode the Republican w=
ave, eking out a tight victory. But with the =0Atide turning, Democrats vie=
w his seat and others Republicans won narrowly two =0Ayears ago as prime pi=
ckup opportunities in November.=0A=0AOther $10 million districts are money =
sinks because the lines were redrawn to =0Agive one party or the other an a=
dvantage. In California, Democrats altered the =0A22nd District to try to o=
ust Republican incumbent David Valadao, who=E2=80=99s =0Arepeatedly survive=
d past elections. As a measure of their commitment, they=E2=80=99ve =0Aouts=
pent Republicans by more than $1 million to make this the second-most =0Aex=
pensive House race in the country.=0A=0AThe situation is reversed in south =
Texas, where the GOP redrew the 34th =0ADistrict with the aim of defeating =
Democratic Representative Vicente Gonzalez. =0AThe new district favored Tru=
mp by roughly 10 percentage points in 2024. But =0Apublic sentiment has shi=
fted so sharply against Republicans that the nonpartisan=0ACook Political R=
eport rates the race as a =E2=80=9Ctoss-up.=E2=80=9D Here again, Democrats =
=0Asmell blood: They=E2=80=99ve outspent Republicans in hopes of keeping Go=
nzalez in =0ACongress.=0A=0AAs with polling, the financial map can shift qu=
ickly, especially in the month =0Abefore the election, as parties are force=
d to make tough decisions about where =0Ato concentrate their spending and =
where to cut bait. Republicans may have =0Abacked off North Carolina=E2=80=
=99s Senate race, but my reading of Pyers=E2=80=99 figures shows =0Athem st=
ill spending significant sums in at least six House districts that =0AKamal=
a Harris won and that are either open seats or have Democratic incumbents.=
